    government: recognise a re-enacted Innovation Office heading
    
    Act 25 codification is required by the enacted bill (v3 section 2.2.1) to use the
    heading '## Act 25 — Executive Innovation Office Act (re-enacted 2026-11-08, bill
    executive-innovation-office-reenactment-act-v3)'. Six detection sites across five
    scripts match the literal '(enacted ' only, so that statutorily mandated heading
    is not recognised: boot.sh takes the legacy pre-enactment arm, the executive
    office cycle does not run, and boot-smoke observes 10 where it expects
    seat_count+1 = 11.
    
    Fix: match '\((re-)?enacted ' at all six sites (boot.sh x2, appointments.sh,
    branch-health.sh, executive-innovation-cycle.sh, sitting.sh). Widening only:
    current law's '(enacted' heading still matches; no assertion relaxed and no
    expectation changed.
    
    The boot-smoke failure was observed on the Clerk draft 6b6d304 whose heading uses
    '(re-enacted ...'. It is not reproducible on main 3ced1f8 only because the
    landed codification used '(enacted ...' instead, which deviates from section
    2.2.1. Rebuilt on current main 3ced1f8.

diff --git a/government/appointments.sh b/government/appointments.sh
index c6b85f5f..43cc1189 100644
--- a/government/appointments.sh
+++ b/government/appointments.sh
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@ if [ -z "$cwd" ]; then
     judiciary) title=Judiciary;;
     innovation-centre)
       title='Legislative Innovation Centre'
-      if grep -Eq '^## Act [0-9]+ — Executive Innovation Office Act \(enacted ' "$town/government/LAWS.md"; then
+      if grep -Eq '^## Act [0-9]+ — Executive Innovation Office Act \((re-)?enacted ' "$town/government/LAWS.md"; then
         title='Executive Innovation Office'
       fi ;;
     recovery-steward) title='Institutional Recovery Steward';;
